examiner (round 1), approach: tests/dependencies-installed.test.ts reads the three manifests from disk at ROOT = one directory above tests/, and encodes the five legs as named tests —
(a) [M1] client/package.json: one test per each of the nine added entries (7 dependencies, 2 devDependencies) asserting the exact range with toBe, and one test per each of the fifteen BASE entries M1 lists (5 deps, 7 devDeps, 3 scripts) still at its BASE value;
(b) [M2] root package.json: one test per each of the four added devDependencies, one for scripts['lint:ui'] === 'node node_modules/eslint/bin/eslint.js client/src' (exact, toBe), and one per each of the eight BASE entries — three packages, four scripts (typecheck pinned by its two ends only, as the Proof says 'by its two ends'), and workspaces by toEqual(['client','server','packages/*']);
(c) [M3] packages/tinyapp-exam/package.json: bun-plugin-tailwind ^0.1.2 and tailwindcss ^4.3.3 under dependencies, plus the four BASE entries;
(d) [M4] one test per each of the thirteen names, each looking for node_modules/<name>/package.json under ROOT, client/ or packages/tinyapp-exam/ and parsing it with readFileSync (never Bun.resolveSync, per the task's context: an exports map may not export ./package.json), asserting the parsed name equals the package's; one further test that the @types/node/package.json so found has a version starting '26.'; and one that 'bun install --frozen-lockfile' spawned at ROOT exits 0;
(e) [M5] 'bun run typecheck' and 'bun run lint:state' each exit 0, one test each.
At BASE the manifest legs are red (no entry exists) and the four spawned Run: legs are green (BASE install/typecheck/lint:state already pass, measured here: 0.01 s / 7.4 s / 2.9 s) — the file's single reason for red is the absent manifest and lockfile work. Spawning tests carry timeouts well above those measurements.
